    "scenesThatPass": [
      "EVEY: At first, the arrests were political. Dissidents. Radicals. Liberals.\nEVEY: When my parents were younger, they had been activists. They had marched with Labor in the great train strike.\nLITTLE EVEY: Mommy?",
      "EVEY: You've made a mistake.\nROSSITER: Shut up.\nEVEY: Please. I haven't done anything --\nROSSITER: I said shut your hole!",
      "EVEY: They were going to rape me, kill me --\nROSSITER: Shut up.",
      "EVEY: No, wait!\nVALERIE: London. I was happy in London.",
      "VALERIE: Not for anybody.\nVALERIE: After the takeover, they started rounding up the gays. They took Ruth while she was out looking for food.\nVALERIE: Why are they so frightened of us?\nVALERIE: They burned her face with cigarettes and made her give them my name. She signed a statement saying I'd seduced her."
    ]
  },
